---
export const prerender = true;
import Shop from '@/layouts/Shop.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '@/components/astro/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { tenant } from '@/config/tenant';

const title = 'Erik Lindqvist — Editor & Lead Product Reviewer, SnusFriend';
const description = 'Erik Lindqvist is the Editor at SnusFriend, specializing in independent nicotine pouch reviews with 4+ years of product testing expertise across 500+ products and 55+ brands.';

const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Erik Lindqvist',
  jobTitle: 'Editor & Lead Product Reviewer',
  worksFor: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'SnusFriend',
    url: `https://${tenant.domain}`,
  },
  description: 'Editor and Lead Product Reviewer at SnusFriend, specializing in European nicotine pouch products with 4+ years of hands-on testing expertise.',
  knowsAbout: ['nicotine pouches', 'tobacco harm reduction', 'smokeless tobacco', 'nicotine pharmacology', 'product testing methodology', 'European nicotine regulation'],
  url: `https://${tenant.domain}/authors/erik-lindqvist`,
  sameAs: [
    'https://www.linkedin.com/in/erik-lindqvist-snusfriend/',
    'https://x.com/ErikAtSnusFriend',
  ],
};
---

<Shop
  title={title}
  description={description}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />

  <article class="bg-background text-foreground">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
      <Breadcrumb items={[
        { label: 'Blog', href: '/blog' },
        { label: 'Erik Lindqvist' },
      ]} />

      <header class="mb-10">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-foreground mb-2">Erik Lindqvist</h1>
        <p class="text-lg font-medium text-primary mb-3">Editor & Lead Product Reviewer, SnusFriend</p>
        <p class="text-base italic text-muted-foreground">4+ years covering European nicotine pouches · 500+ products tested · Scandinavia-based</p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex gap-4">
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/erik-lindqvist-snusfriend/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground underline">LinkedIn</a>
          <a href="https://x.com/ErikAtSnusFriend" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground underline">X / Twitter</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground [&_h2]:text-foreground [&_h2]:text-2xl [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-4 [&_h3]:text-foreground [&_h3]:text-xl [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:mt-8 [&_h3]:mb-3 [&_strong]:text-foreground [&_a]:text-primary [&_a]:underline [&_a:hover]:text-foreground [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ul]:space-y-1 [&_li]:leading-relaxed">

        <p>
          Erik Lindqvist is the Editor and Lead Product Reviewer at SnusFriend, specializing in the European nicotine pouch market. Based in Scandinavia — the heartland of the industry — he brings four years of hands-on product expertise and a background in consumer health communication.
        </p>

        <p>
          Since launching his review practice in 2022, Erik has personally tested over 500 nicotine pouch products across 55+ brands, combining blind taste testing with rigorous cross-referencing of manufacturer specifications and independent lab data. His editorial approach emphasizes transparency and evidence-based assessment in an industry where traditional advertising restrictions mean consumers depend heavily on independent reviewers to make informed choices.
        </p>

        <p>
          Erik's work bridges product journalism and consumer advocacy. He attends harm reduction conferences, follows EU TPD regulatory developments, and maintains strict editorial standards: no paid reviews, transparent affiliate disclosure, and a public corrections policy.
        </p>

        <h2>How Erik Got Into Nicotine Pouch Reviewing</h2>

        <p>
          Erik didn't set out to become a nicotine pouch expert. In 2022, he was working in consumer health communication when the Nordic nicotine pouch market began its global expansion. He noticed something: enthusiasts and newcomers alike were making purchasing decisions based on hearsay, forum rumors, and marketing speak — not actual product data.
        </p>

        <p>
          The category was exploding, but independent, trustworthy reviews barely existed. Traditional consumer media ignored it. Manufacturer websites were predictably biased. Harm reduction researchers published sparse, outdated comparisons. There was a real gap.
        </p>

        <p>
          He started testing products for personal use, then sharing findings in online communities. The response was immediate: people wanted rigorous, honest assessments. That experimental project became a systematic practice, and eventually led to founding SnusFriend's editorial review program.
        </p>

        <h2>Testing Methodology</h2>

        <p>Every SnusFriend review follows a documented protocol:</p>

        <p>
          <strong>1. Blind testing</strong> — Products are evaluated without seeing packaging or marketing claims.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>2. Multi-day windows</strong> — Each product is tested across 3–7 days to capture consistency and subjective variation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>3. Cross-referencing</strong> — Manufacturer specs are verified against independent lab data where publicly available; discrepancies are flagged.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>4. Comparative context</strong> — Products are assessed relative to similar offerings, not in isolation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>5. Revision cycles</strong> — Reviews are updated when new formulations launch or additional testing reveals relevant information.
        </p>

        <p>
          This approach trades speed for depth. We publish fewer reviews than clickbait competitors, but each one is designed to remain useful for years.
        </p>

        <h2>Credentials</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>4+ years covering the European nicotine pouch market (since 2022)</li>
          <li>500+ products personally tested across 55+ brands</li>
          <li>Scandinavia-based — direct proximity to market innovation and regulatory environment</li>
          <li>Background in consumer health communication</li>
          <li>Health content fact-checked against peer-reviewed PubMed research, NHS guidance, and WHO reports</li>
          <li>Follows EU Tobacco Products Directive (TPD) regulatory developments</li>
          <li>Editorial independence: no brand pays for product placement or favourable reviews</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>No paid reviews.</strong> Manufacturers cannot pay for favorable coverage. Affiliate links are disclosed.</li>
          <li><strong>Transparent corrections.</strong> Errors are acknowledged publicly with publication dates.</li>
          <li><strong>Conflict of interest disclosure.</strong> SnusFriend is a retailer — we sell the products Erik reviews. We acknowledge this openly.</li>
          <li><strong>Reader feedback loop.</strong> We actively solicit corrections from readers with direct product experience.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why Independent Reviews Matter</h2>

        <p>
          In most consumer goods categories, advertising is abundant. Nicotine products face severe restrictions. In the EU, manufacturers cannot run traditional ads. Consumers can't rely on the usual sources of product information.
        </p>

        <p>
          That shifts responsibility to independent reviewers. We're not just sharing opinions — we're functioning as a trusted information infrastructure in a category where it barely exists. That's why our standards are strict and our methodology is transparent.
        </p>

        <h2>The SnusFriend Team</h2>

        <p>
          Erik leads editorial but doesn't work alone. SnusFriend's review system includes cross-checking, multiple perspectives, and community feedback. Our goal is a reference resource that reflects genuine consumer experience, not individual taste.
        </p>

        <p>
          When you read an Erik Lindqvist review, you're reading one person's methodology applied consistently — but informed by a team that cares about getting it right.
        </p>

        <h2>Articles by Erik Lindqvist</h2>

        <p>
          Erik authors and edits all long-form health, harm reduction, and product review content on SnusFriend. His articles cover nicotine pharmacology, product comparisons, strength guides, and regulatory updates — all grounded in peer-reviewed research and independent testing.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/blog">Browse all articles on the SnusFriend blog</a>
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Shop>
